class:: InterchannelPhase
summary:: Circular mean of interchannel spectral phase
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/FFT

description::
Averages L*conj(R) for each FFT bin over time, then sums cross spectra in the selected band. The phase is atan2(imaginary, real), and concentration is the magnitude of that vector divided by the sum of individual cross-spectrum magnitudes. Positive phase means the left channel leads the right. Low concentration indicates contradictory frequency-bin phases; silence returns zero for both outputs. This is a band phase statistic, not a time-delay estimate.

Uses two private radix-2 FFTs and precomputed Hann windows. frameSize and hop are fixed at construction. CPU is O(frameSize*log(frameSize)) per hop; all storage is allocated before processing. First output is available after frameSize/sampleRate, with coherence held at zero for another three hops; reliable averaging takes approximately averageTime. Frequency selection is quantized to FFT bins. Source for the cross-spectral definition: link::https://www.mathworks.com/help/signal/ref/mscohere.html::.

Vanilla FFT exposes separate spectral frames; this UGen combines two channels and maintains cross-spectral averages.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: frameSize
Literal FFT power of two, 256..8192.

argument:: hop
Literal frame fraction, 0.0625..1; default 0.5.

argument:: averageTime
Exponential spectral averaging constant, clipped to 0.01..10 seconds.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; zero means Nyquist.

returns::
Array [phaseRadians, phaseConcentration], with phase in -pi..pi and concentration in 0..1.

examples::
InterchannelPhase computes the circular mean of the interchannel spectral phase in radians (-pi to +pi) and its phase concentration (0 to 1). In this example, measured phase difference controls an allpass phase-correction delay line, dynamically aligning phase differences between stereo channels. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: displays real-time interchannel phase in radians.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("stereo.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.isKindOf(Buffer) and: { ~mir2Buffer.numChannels >= 2 }) {
            PlayBuf.ar(2, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
                var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
                [sig, DelayC.ar(sig, 0.02, 0.003)]
            } {
                // Synthetic stereo fallback
                var l = Saw.ar(220) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                var r = Saw.ar(222) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                [l, r]
            }
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);

        var phaseData = InterchannelPhase.kr(source[0], source[1], frameSize: 1024, hop: 0.5, averageTime: 0.1, minFreq: 150, maxFreq: 4000);
        var phaseRad = phaseData[0].lag(0.08);
        var phaseDelay = phaseRad.linlin(-pi, pi, 0.0001, 0.002).clip(0.0001, 0.005);
        var correctedR = AllpassC.ar(source[1], 0.01, phaseDelay, 0.05);
        var sound = [source[0], correctedR] * 0.25;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, phaseRad) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Interchannel Phase", ~mir2Bus, -pi, pi, "rad");
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

